%% Trust boundaries. Model/agent/web output is untrusted input. Security is architectural (L30).
%% See ../SECURITY_MODEL.md.
flowchart TB
    subgraph U["UNTRUSTED — validate before ANY influence"]
        WEB[Web / fetched content\ntagged origin + untrusted]
        MO[Model output]
        AO[Agent output — pre-validation]
        EXT[External API responses]
        GN[Guest / mobile node input]
    end

    subgraph S["SEMI-TRUSTED — authenticated · scoped · sandboxed"]
        GW[Model Gateway\nholds provider keys ONLY]
        AD[Capability adapters\nown scoped resource cred ONLY]
        PP[Perception processes\npublish jarvis.perception.> ONLY]
        ND[Owned nodes\ndeclared trust tier]
    end

    subgraph T["TRUSTED — the spine"]
        K[Kernel components]
        PE[Policy + Permission Engines\ndeterministic]
        DB[(PostgreSQL: events · projections · world_model · memory · audit)]
        AU[Audit Manager — append-only]
    end

    U -->|Validator: schema + safety + provenance tagging| S
    S -->|typed contracts + events + scoped creds| T
    MO -. holds NO credentials · cannot call capabilities · cannot write state\n=> jailbreak escalates to nothing .-> K
    WEB -. any Proposal derived from this => derivedFromUntrusted=true\n=> cannot justify action > riskClass LOW .-> PE

    subgraph creds["Credential partitioning"]
        c1[Kernel: DB + NATS(ledger) creds]
        c2[Gateway: provider API keys]
        c3[Each adapter: its own scoped resource cred]
        c4[Agents: NOTHING]
        c5[Experience surfaces: scoped session token]
    end
